  "title": "Baked Feta (Feta Psiti)",
  "description": null,
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Baked Feta (Psiti) is a traditional Greek dish. It is very easy to prepare at home and will become one of your favorite <a href=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/recipes/appetizers/\">appetizers</a>.  </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21506,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1609288453692} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21506-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Baked Feta (Feta Psiti)</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/IMG_9891.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\t\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>200 g feta cheese ((in one block))</li><li>2 pinches oregano</li><li>Some chili pepper flakes</li><li>1 Tbsp olive oil</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>Preheat oven to 400F.</li><li>Place the feta in an oven-proof dish. Add the oregano and chili pepper flakes followed by the olive oil.</li><li>Bake for 8-10 minutes.</li><li>Serve hot with fresh bread or pita.</li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
